    <statement><p>Evaluate the integral below by interpreting it in terms of areas. In other words, draw a picture of the region the integral represents,
and find the area using high school geometry.</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle \int_{-2}^{2} \sqrt{4 - x^2 } \; dx =</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
